summary: Checks the output of the auxiliary vectors to ensure the values are not changing
    on new kernel updates or installs.
description: |
        This test checks the output of the auxiliary vectors to ensure the values are not changing on new kernel updates or installs.
        These values should be the same provided the hardware has not changed.

        User can provide custom TYPE and VALUE lists through variables:
        AUXILIARY_TYPES
        AUXILIARY_VALUES
        It allows the user to pick which TYPES to report on.
        NOTE:   It is important to make sure type and value are at the same index in each list. So the first type must match the first value and so on to the last.
                The user must set VAR_HWCAP, VAR_HWCAP2 and VAR_PLATFORM for the test defaults to work.

        By default:
            AUXILIARY_TYPES="AT_HWCAP AT_HWCAP2 AT_PLATFORM"
            AUXILIARY_VALUES="${VAR_HWCAP} ${VAR_HWCAP2} ${VAR_PLATFORM}"
contact: Stephen Bertram <sbertram@redhat.com>
id: 38286610-074c-439c-bc1f-37882149502a
test: bash ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
duration: 10m
